N logitfe.pkg
D  2 Jun 2021
U 19
d 'LOGITFE': module to compute analytical and jackknife bias corrections for fixed effects estimators of panel logit models with individual and time effects
d 
d  logitfe fits a logit fixed-effects estimator that can include
d individual and/or time effects, and account for both the bias
d arising from the inclusion of individual fixed-effects and/or the
d bias arising from the inclusion of time fixed-effects. logitfe
d with the nocorrection option does not correct for the incidental
d parameter bias problem (Neyman and Scott, 1948). logitfe with the
d analytical option removes an analytical estimate of the bias from
d the logit fixed-effects estimator using the expressions derived
d in Fernandez-Val and Weidner (2016). The trimming parameter can
d be set to any value between 0 and (T-1), where T is the number of
d time periods. logitfe with the jackknife option removes a
d jackknife estimate of the bias from the fixed effects estimator.
d This method is based on the delete-one panel jackknife of Hahn
d and Newey (2004) and split panel jackknife of Dhaene and Jochmans
d (2010) as described in Fernandez-Val and Weidner (2016). logitfe
d displays estimates of Index Coefficients and Average Partial
d Effects.
d 
d KW: logit
d KW: fixed effects
d KW: bias corrections
d KW: panel
d KW: jackknife
d 
d Requires: Stata version 11.2 and moremata from SSC (q.v.)
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20170310
d 
d Author: Mario Cruz-Gonzalez,  Boston University
d Support: email mgonza@@bu.edu
d 
d Author: Ivan Fernandez-Val ,  Boston University
d Support: email
d 
d Author:  Martin Weidner , University College London
d Support: email
d 
f l\logitfe.ado
f l\logitfe.sthlp
e
