N shufflevar.pkg
D 23 Jun 2025
U 61
d 'SHUFFLEVAR': module to shuffle variables relative to the rest of the dataset
d 
d  shufflevar takes varlist and either jointly or for each variable
d shuffles varlist relative to the rest of the dataset. This means
d any  association between varlist and the rest of the dataset will
d be random.  Much like bootstrap or the Quadratic Assignment
d Procedure (QAP), one can build a distribution of results out of
d randomness to serve as a baseline  against which to compare
d empirical results, especially for overall model-fit  or
d clustering measures.
d 
d KW: shuffle
d KW: random
d KW: reorder
d 
d Requires: Stata version 10
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20110125
d 
d Author: Gabriel Rossman, UCLA
d Support: email rossman@@soc.ucla.edu
d 
f s\shufflevar.ado
f s\shufflevar.sthlp
e
S http://fmwww.bc.edu/repec/bocode/b
N b1x2.pkg
D 26 Jun 2025
U 62
d 'B1X2': module to account for changes when X2 is added to a base model with X1
d 
d  b1x2 runs a "base" regression, runs a "full" regression with an
d additional regressor, and computes both the difference in the
d coefficent estimates for x1all     (including the constant) and a
d consistent estimate of the  asymptotic covariance matrix for
d this difference.
d 
d KW: regression
d KW: variance accounting
d 
d Requires: Stata version 10
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20140330
d 
d Author: Jonah Gelbach, University of Arizona
d Support: email gelbach@@gmail.com
d 
f b\b1x2.ado
f b\b1x2.sthlp
e
